## Component Creation & Structure

### Standalone-Only Architecture

- **No NgModules.** All components, directives, and pipes are standalone.
- `standalone: true` is **implicit** in Angular 21 — do **NOT** set it explicitly in decorators.

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG — do not write standalone: true
@Component({
    standalone: true,
    selector: 'app-partner',
    ...
})

// ✅ CORRECT — standalone is implied
@Component({
    selector: 'app-partner',
    ...
})
```

### Inline Templates (Mandatory for New Components)

All new components must use **inline templates** (`template:`) and inline or no styles. Do NOT use `templateUrl` or `styleUrl`.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — inline template
@Component({
    selector: 'app-partner',
    imports: [CommonModule, ButtonModule, TableModule, TranslateModule],
    changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
    template: `
        <div class="card">
            @if (isLoading()) {
                <p-skeleton />
            } @else {
                <p-table [value]="partners()">
                    <!-- table content -->
                </p-table>
            }
        </div>
    `
})
export class Partner { }

// ❌ WRONG — external template files
@Component({
    selector: 'app-partner',
    templateUrl: './partner.component.html',
    styleUrl: './partner.component.scss',
})
export class PartnerComponent { }
```

SCSS files are still acceptable alongside inline templates for complex patterns that Tailwind cannot express, but should be minimal.

### Dependency Injection: Use `inject()`

Prefer the `inject()` function over constructor injection for all new code.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — inject() function
export class Partner {
    private readonly partnerService = inject(PartnerService);
    private readonly feedbackService = inject(FeedbackDialogService);
    private readonly router = inject(Router);
}

// ❌ WRONG — constructor injection
export class PartnerComponent {
    constructor(
        private partnerService: PartnerService,
        private feedbackService: FeedbackDialogService,
        private router: Router
    ) { }
}
```

### Change Detection

- The UX reference app uses `provideZonelessChangeDetection()` globally.
- This app currently uses `provideZoneChangeDetection({ eventCoalescing: true })`.
- For new components, always use `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` to prepare for eventual zoneless migration.
- Use signals for all reactive state — do NOT rely on Zone.js change detection triggers.

### Templates — Modern Control Flow

- Use `@if`, `@for`, `@switch` — do NOT use `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`.
- Use `[class.active]="condition"` or `[class]="{'active': condition}"` — do NOT use `ngClass`.
- Use `[style.font-size.px]="value"` — do NOT use `ngStyle`.

### Naming Convention & Folder Structure

**MANDATORY**: Follow this consistent naming and folder organization pattern for all entity components.

**CRITICAL**: All folder and file names MUST use **kebab-case**.

**File Naming** (for NEW components):
- File: `entity-name.ts` (no `.component.ts` suffix)
- Class: `export class EntityName` (no `Component` suffix)
- Selector: `app-entity-name`

**Existing** components using `.component.ts` / `Component` suffix do not need to be renamed. All **new** code follows the simplified convention.

**Pattern Structure:**
```
entity-name/
├── entity-name.ts                            # List/overview component
├── entity-name.scss                          # Optional — only for complex patterns
├── entity-name-item/                         # Detail component folder
│   └── entity-name-item.ts
├── new-entity-name/                          # Create dialog component folder
│   └── new-entity-name.ts
├── delete-entity-name/                       # Other dialog components
│   └── delete-entity-name.ts
├── custom-action-entity-name/                # Custom action dialogs
│   └── custom-action-entity-name.ts
└── child-entity/                             # Child entities (recursive pattern)
    ├── child-entity.ts
    ├── child-entity-item/
    │   └── child-entity-item.ts
    ├── new-child-entity/
    │   └── new-child-entity.ts
    └── delete-child-entity/
        └── delete-child-entity.ts
```

**Real-World Example - Partner Entity:**
```
partner/
├── partner.ts                                # Partner list component
├── partner.scss                              # Optional SCSS
├── partner-item/
│   └── partner-item.ts
├── new-partner/
│   └── new-partner.ts
├── delete-partner/
│   └── delete-partner.ts
└── contacts/                                 # Child entity (recursive)
    ├── contacts.ts
    ├── contact-item/
    │   └── contact-item.ts
    ├── new-contact/
    │   └── new-contact.ts
    └── delete-contact/
        └── delete-contact.ts
```

**Naming Rules:**

1. **List Component**: `entity-name.ts`
   - Selector: `app-entity-name` (e.g., `app-partner`, `app-opportunity`)

2. **Detail Component**: `entity-name-item/entity-name-item.ts`
   - Selector: `app-entity-name-item` (e.g., `app-partner-item`)

3. **Create Dialog**: `new-entity-name/new-entity-name.ts`
   - Selector: `app-new-entity-name` (e.g., `app-new-partner`)

4. **Other Dialogs**: `action-entity-name/action-entity-name.ts`
   - **CRITICAL**: Dialog names MUST include the entity name (not generic names)
   - Pattern: `{action}-{entity-name}` in kebab-case
   - Example: `partner/delete-partner/delete-partner.ts` (NOT `delete-confirmation-dialog`)
   - **Note**: Edit functionality is handled by `entity-name-item` component, not a separate dialog

5. **Child Entities**: Follow same pattern recursively inside parent folder

**Component Selector Naming:**
- Always prefix with `app-`
- Use kebab-case matching folder/file name
- ESLint config should enforce `prefix: 'app'` (not `'p'`)

