## Permission Handling

### MANDATORY: Server-Side Permission Checks Only

**CRITICAL**: NEVER manually handle permissions on the client side. ALL permission checks must be performed server-side via dedicated permission endpoints.

### Correct Pattern — Server-Side Permission Endpoint

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — Component TypeScript
export class PartnerItem {
    private readonly partnerService = inject(PartnerService);

    readonly recordPermissions = signal<any>(null);
    readonly permissionsLoading = signal(false);

    readonly canEdit = computed(() => this.recordPermissions()?.canEdit === true);
    readonly canDelete = computed(() => this.recordPermissions()?.canDelete === true);
    readonly canChangeStage = computed(() => {
        const permissions = this.recordPermissions();
        return permissions?.canActivate === true || permissions?.canCancel === true;
    });

    ngOnInit(): void {
        this.loadRecord();
        this.loadPermissions();
    }

    private loadPermissions(): void {
        this.permissionsLoading.set(true);
        this.partnerService.getRecordDetailPermissionsById(this.recordId).subscribe({
            next: (data: any) => {
                this.recordPermissions.set(data);
                this.permissionsLoading.set(false);
            },
            error: () => {
                this.permissionsLoading.set(false);
            }
        });
    }
}
```

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — Service with permission endpoint
export class PartnerService {
    private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);

    getRecordDetailPermissionsById(recordId: string): Observable<any> {
        this.isLoading.set(true);
        return this.http.get(`/api/partner/${recordId}/permissions`).pipe(
            tap({
                next: () => this.isLoading.set(false),
                error: () => this.isLoading.set(false)
            })
        );
    }
}
```

```html
<!-- ✅ CORRECT — Use computed permissions in template -->
<div class="flex gap-2">
    @if (canEdit()) {
        <p-button
            [label]="'button.edit' | translate"
            icon="pi pi-pencil"
            severity="primary"
            (onClick)="onEdit()"
        />
    }
    @if (canDelete()) {
        <p-button
            [label]="'button.delete' | translate"
            icon="pi pi-trash"
            severity="danger"
            (onClick)="onDelete()"
        />
    }
</div>
```

### Incorrect Patterns — DO NOT DO THIS

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG — Manual client-side permission logic
canEdit = computed(() => {
    const currentUser = this.authService.currentUser();
    const isOwner = this.record()?.createdBy === currentUser.id;
    return isOwner && this.record()?.stage === 'Draft';
});

// ❌ WRONG — Hardcoded permission flags
canEdit = signal(true);

// ❌ WRONG — Role-based checks in component
canApprove = computed(() => this.authService.hasRole('Administrator'));
```

### Permission Endpoint Pattern

**Standard URL:** `GET /api/{entity-name}/{recordId}/permissions`

**Standard Response:**
```json
{
    "canEdit": true,
    "canDelete": false,
    "canSubmit": true,
    "canApprove": false,
    "canActivate": true,
    "canCancel": false,
    "canReview": true
}
```

### Permission Integration Checklist

- [ ] Add `recordPermissions` signal to store server response
- [ ] Add `permissionsLoading` signal for loading state
- [ ] Create computed signals for each permission flag
- [ ] Add service method `getRecordDetailPermissionsById(recordId: string)`
- [ ] Call `loadPermissions()` in `ngOnInit()`
- [ ] Reload permissions after state-changing actions
- [ ] Use computed permission signals in template with `@if` conditions
- [ ] **NEVER** manually check roles, user ID, or entity state for permissions
- [ ] **ALWAYS** get permissions from server endpoint

