## Workflow Component Usage

### MANDATORY: Use Workflow Component for All Workflow-Related UI

**CRITICAL**: Always use the `app-workflow` component for displaying workflow stages and actions. NEVER create separate buttons or display stage status independently.

### Correct Pattern

```typescript
import { WorkflowComponent } from '@shared/reusables/components/workflow/components/workflow/workflow.component';

@Component({
    selector: 'app-opportunity-item',
    imports: [WorkflowComponent],
    template: `
        @if (!isLoading()) {
            <app-workflow
                [entityName]="'opportunity'"
                [entityId]="opportunityId().toString()"
                [canChangeStage]="canChangeStage()"
                [beforeStageChange]="beforeStageChange"
                (onStageChangeSuccess)="handleStageChangeSuccess()"
            />
        }
    `
})
export class OpportunityItem {
    opportunityId = signal<number>(0);
    readonly canChangeStage = signal(false);

    handleStageChangeSuccess(): void {
        this.loadOpportunity();
    }

    beforeStageChange = async (nextStage: string): Promise<boolean> => {
        if (this.hasUnsavedChanges()) {
            return await this.feedbackService.confirm({
                title: 'Unsaved Changes',
                message: 'You have unsaved changes. Do you want to continue?'
            });
        }
        return true;
    };
}
```

### Component Inputs and Outputs

**Required Inputs:**
- `entityName` (string): Entity type identifier (e.g., `'opportunity'`, `'partner'`)
- `entityId` (string): Unique identifier (must be converted to string)

**Optional Inputs:**
- `canChangeStage` (boolean): Whether the user can perform workflow actions (default: `true`)
- `beforeStageChange` (function): `(nextStage: string) => Promise<boolean>` — return `true` to allow

**Outputs:**
- `onStageChangeSuccess`: Emitted when a stage change is completed successfully

### Dialog Components — Separation Pattern

**MANDATORY**: All dialogs (`p-dialog`) must be extracted into separate dedicated dialog components.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — Dialog in separate component
@Component({
    selector: 'app-new-partner',
    imports: [DialogModule, ReactiveFormsModule, ButtonModule],
    template: `
        <p-dialog [(visible)]="visible" (onHide)="visibleChange.emit(false)">
            <form [formGroup]="form" (ngSubmit)="onSubmit()">
                <!-- Dialog content -->
            </form>
        </p-dialog>
    `
})
export class NewPartner {
    readonly visible = model<boolean>(false);
    readonly partnerCreated = output<PartnerModel>();
}

// ✅ Parent component uses dialog as a child
@Component({
    selector: 'app-partner',
    imports: [NewPartner, ButtonModule, TableModule],
    template: `
        <div>
            <p-button (onClick)="showCreateDialog = true" />
            <app-new-partner
                [(visible)]="showCreateDialog"
                (partnerCreated)="onPartnerCreated($event)"
            />
        </div>
    `
})
export class Partner {
    showCreateDialog = false;
}
```

**Exception:** Very simple confirmations — use `FeedbackDialogService` instead.

