## Tailwind-First Styling

### Template Styling

**MANDATORY**: Use Tailwind classes directly in templates, NOT custom CSS classes.

```html
<!-- ✅ CORRECT — standard Tailwind / PrimeNG token utilities -->
<div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-4 p-6 bg-surface-card rounded-md shadow-sm border border-surface-border">
    <button class="bg-primary text-white px-6 py-2 rounded-md hover:bg-primary-emphasis transition-colors duration-200">
        {{ text() }}
    </button>
</div>
```

### No Hardcoded Visual Values

| Avoid | Prefer |
|-------|--------|
| `color: #0092d1` | `var(--color-darkblue-500)` or `text-darkblue-500` |
| `background: #ffffff` | `var(--surface-card)` or `bg-white` |
| `padding: 16px` | Tailwind `p-4` |
| `font-size: 14px` | Tailwind `text-sm` |
| `border-radius: 8px` | Tailwind `rounded-md` |
| `unops-*` utilities | Standard Tailwind names (`text-darkblue-500`, `bg-gray-50`) — the `unops-*` prefix utilities do not exist |

### Dark Mode

- Single CSS class: `.app-dark` on `<html>`
- PrimeNG: `darkModeSelector: '.app-dark'`
- Tailwind: `@custom-variant dark (.app-dark)` in `tailwind.css`
- Custom responsive variants: `unops-mobile:`, `unops-tablet:`, `unops-desktop:` (defined in `tailwind.css`)

### SCSS Only for Complex Patterns

Use SCSS sparingly, only for patterns that Tailwind cannot express. Minimal component-scoped SCSS is acceptable.

